  "cli_result_text": "## Cross-repo trace: FastAPI request body \u2192 Pydantic v2 discriminated-union resolution\n\n**1. FastAPI: dependency injection \u2192 body parameter solving**\n\n- `fastapi/routing.py` (`get_request_handler`): reads the raw HTTP body (`await request.body()`), and \u2014 for JSON content \u2014 parses it via `json.loads` into a Python dict (`body_bytes` \u2192 `body`), then calls `solve_dependencies(..., body=body, ...)`.\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py::solve_dependencies`: for each `Dependant.body_params`, calls `await request_body_to_args(required_params=dependant.body_params, received_body=body)`.\n- `fastapi/dependencies/utils.py::request_body_to_args`: pulls the sub-value for the body field out of the parsed dict (`received_body.get(field.alias)`), then calls `field.validate(value, values, loc=loc)` \u2014 this is the FastAPI\u2192Pydantic handoff.\n- `fastapi/_compat.py::ModelField.validate` (Pydantic v2 branch): delegates to `self._type_adapter.validate_python(value, from_attributes=True)`, where `self._type_adapter` is a `pydantic.TypeAdapter` built once in `ModelField.__post_init__` from `Annotated[field_info.annotation, field_info]`. **This is the exact boundary** \u2014 FastAPI hands a plain dict to Pydantic-core validation here, and any `ValidationError` raised inside is caught and turned into FastAPI's 422 errors (`_regenerate_error_with_loc`). If no `ValidationError` is raised, FastAPI has no way to know a field was silently defaulted.\n\n**2. Pydantic v2: discriminated-union schema construction and model_validator ordering**\n\n- `pydantic/_internal/_generate_schema.py`: `_model_schema` builds the model's core schema, and `apply_model_validators(schema, decorators.model_validators.values(), 'outer'|'all')` wraps that schema with each `@model_validator`. In the wrapping logic (`chunk ~34`), `mode == 'before'` validators are applied via `no_info_before_validator_function`/`with_info_before_validator_function`, wrapping **outside** the inner model-fields/tagged-union schema \u2014 i.e., a `before` validator's function is the *first* thing to touch the raw input dict, before pydantic-core even builds the union schema's field lookup.\n- `pydantic/functional_validators.py::model_validator` / `ModelBeforeValidator` protocols: confirm `mode='before'` validators receive the raw input value (`dict`, model instance, or anything passed to `validate_python`/`validate_json`) and return a (possibly mutated) value that becomes the new input to the rest of the schema.\n- `pydantic/_internal/_discriminated_union.py::apply_discriminator` / `_ApplyInferredDiscriminator`: converts a `Union[...]` annotated with `discriminator=...` into a `tagged-union` core schema. It walks each variant's core schema, extracts the `Literal` value of the discriminator field (`_infer_discriminator_values_for_choice` \u2192 `_infer_discriminator_values_for_field`), and builds a `discriminator value \u2192 variant schema` map executed by pydantic-core's Rust tagged-union validator. Critically, this validator looks up the discriminator key **directly in whatever dict it's handed** \u2014 it has no visibility into, and runs strictly *after*, any outer `model_validator(mode='before')`.\n\n**3. Why the field silently becomes `None`**\n\nThe wrapping order is: `model_validator(mode='before')` \u2192 (inner) model-fields schema \u2192 tagged-union field validator. If the customer's `before` validator pre-processes the incoming JSON (e.g., renaming/normalizing keys, or reconstructing a `dict` via something like `data.pop(...)`/`{k: v for k, v in data.items() if ...}`) and in doing so drops or renames the discriminator key (e.g., `\"type\"` / `\"kind\"`) before returning the dict, the tagged-union validator inside pydantic-core receives a dict *without* the key it needs to select a variant.\n\nPydantic-core's tagged-union schema is built with `strict=False` and, depending on whether a `default` was declared on the discriminated-union field, missing-discriminator resolution can fall through to whichever branch is structurally compatible or to the field's default \u2014 producing `None` for the union field with no `ValidationError` raised, rather than the `discriminator-no-field`/`union_tag_not_found` error that occurs when there's no default. Because no exception propagates, `fastapi/_compat.py::ModelField.validate` returns `(value, None)` (no errors), `request_body_to_args` never appends to `errors`, and `solve_dependencies` proceeds \u2014 so FastAPI returns 200 with the discriminated field silently `None`, instead of a 422.\n\n**Root cause, precisely stated:** the `model_validator(mode='before')` sits *outside* pydantic-core's tagged-union resolution in the wrapping order established by `pydantic/_internal/_generate_schema.py::apply_model_validators`. Any key-stripping/renaming logic in that before-validator that doesn't preserve the discriminator field name pydantic-core expects (`pydantic/_internal/_discriminated_union.py`'s inferred `self.discriminator`/`self._discriminator_alias`) breaks discriminator lookup invisibly, and FastAPI's integration boundary (`fastapi/_compat.py::ModelField.validate`) only surfaces problems that pydantic-core reports as a `ValidationError` \u2014 a variant that resolves to `None` via a default is not one of those.",
